From: =?UTF-8?q?Eduardo=20Garc=C3=ADa-M=C3=A1dico=20Portabella?=
 <woodyst@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 18 Jul 2026 00:11:12 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 059/106] media: qcom: camss: add a runtime-tunable settle
 delay after arming CSIPHY

csiphy_stream_on() returns the instant the lane-enable registers are
written, with no settle time before video_start_streaming() walks on to
call the sensor's own s_stream(1) (VFE -> CSID -> CSIPHY -> sensor,
sensor last). On the vendor's Android stack that gap is whatever CamX's
userspace HAL takes between the separate "configure CSIPHY" and "start
sensor" ioctls - invisible to us here, and not necessarily zero.

Diagnostic tool for the sm7150 CSIPHY silent-capture investigation (both
sensors emit, CSID sees 0 packets and 0 errors): a runtime-writable
parameter to test whether a settle gap changes anything, without
rebuilding between attempts.
/sys/module/qcom_camss/parameters/csiphy_settle_delay_us

Tested up to 20ms (three orders of magnitude past any real D-PHY analog
settle time) on a real IMX682 capture attempt: TOTAL_PKTS_RCVD and
TOTAL_CRC_ERR stay at 0 regardless. Rules out pipeline bring-up timing as
the cause. Defaults to 0 (off) - zero behavior change until written.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 .../media/platform/qcom/camss/camss-csiphy.c  | 20 +++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 20 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/media/platform/qcom/camss/camss-csiphy.c b/drivers/media/platform/qcom/camss/camss-csiphy.c
index 7979890ec..0418812ba 100644
--- a/drivers/media/platform/qcom/camss/camss-csiphy.c
+++ b/drivers/media/platform/qcom/camss/camss-csiphy.c
@@ -13,11 +13,28 @@
 #include <linux/interrupt.h>
 #include <linux/io.h>
 #include <linux/kernel.h>
+#include <linux/module.h>
 #include <linux/of.h>
 #include <linux/platform_device.h>
 #include <linux/pm_runtime.h>
 #include <media/media-entity.h>
 #include <media/v4l2-device.h>
+
+/*
+ * csiphy_stream_on() returns the instant the lane-enable registers are
+ * written, with no settle time before the v4l2 pipeline walks on to call
+ * the sensor's own s_stream(1) (see video_start_streaming() in
+ * camss-video.c: VFE -> CSID -> CSIPHY -> sensor, sensor last). On the
+ * vendor's Android stack that gap is whatever CamX's userspace HAL takes
+ * between the separate "configure CSIPHY" and "start sensor" ioctls -
+ * invisible to us, and not necessarily zero. Runtime-tunable in
+ * microseconds to test without rebuilding:
+ * /sys/module/qcom_camss/parameters/csiphy_settle_delay_us
+ */
+static uint csiphy_settle_delay_us;
+module_param(csiphy_settle_delay_us, uint, 0644);
+MODULE_PARM_DESC(csiphy_settle_delay_us,
+		 "Delay after arming CSIPHY lanes, before the sensor is allowed to stream (us)");
 #include <media/v4l2-subdev.h>
 
 #include "camss-csiphy.h"
@@ -298,6 +315,9 @@ static int csiphy_stream_on(struct csiphy_device *csiphy)
 
 	csiphy->res->hw_ops->lanes_enable(csiphy, cfg, link_freq, lane_mask);
 
+	if (csiphy_settle_delay_us)
+		usleep_range(csiphy_settle_delay_us, csiphy_settle_delay_us + 500);
+
 	return 0;
 }
 
